SYNTHETIC DATA PROVENANCE

The sample data in setup/data/ is generated by setup/generate_data.py using
Python's standard library, including the random module with a fixed seed of 7.
The script generates equipment, plants, work orders, alarms, parts catalogs,
and vendor records, and calculates expected answers in expected.json.

The generated dataset is a fixed historical demonstration snapshot from
October 1, 2025 through October 25, 2026. It deliberately includes data-quality
and interpretation challenges, including work orders closed with no fault
found and downtime recorded in seconds instead of minutes before a specified
software-fix date. These scenarios demonstrate cross-conversation memory;
they are not observations of real plant operations.

Cascade Fabrication and its technician personas are fictional. No customer
records, production maintenance logs, or third-party datasets were used to
generate the sample records. The generation code is included so readers can
inspect and reproduce the dataset:

    uv run python setup/generate_data.py

Some manufacturer, supplier, and product names refer to real organizations
or products. All sample fault behavior, prices, lead times, reliability
statements, and repair outcomes are invented for this demonstration. They
are not factual assessments of those organizations or products and do not
imply endorsement or affiliation.

Seed conversations in setup/seed_conversations.py are authored demonstration
scenarios. Agent responses, extracted memories, and evaluation scores are
model-generated test artifacts, not customer evidence or guaranteed results.

